I just read a note from someone who is very frustrated with nethack -- seems
he is getting frustrated by being killed.

I have the perfect solution -- CHEAT!

How do I cheat?  I save my game, and then copy the save file.  When I
get killed, I copy the saved file back into the playground, and pick
up where I left off.

This isn't possible in Unix installations, unless the system
administrator gives write permission to the save directory.

There are probably many who think this is a terrible practice, but
hold your flames.  I AM impressed by people who win without cheating,
but I think cheating is in the spirit of the game.  How could someone
win from scratch without reading rec.games.hack anyway? (including all
the spoilers) Isn't that cheating?  And what about this business of
robbing shops?  If you are morally pure, you would wander around
collecting gold until you could AFFORD all that junk.

Once you've won with cheating, you can then ascend to the next plateau
-- winning without cheating.

